<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24968" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrĕvĕrentĭa</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inr-</span></b> ),
		ae, f.
		irreverens, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>want of due respect</i> or <i>reverence</i>, <i>irreverence</i>, <i>disrespect</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coalitam libertate irreverentiam prorupisse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 13, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juventutis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 31</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adversus, fas nefasque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					3, 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">studiorum,</span>”
				<i>inattention to</i>, <i>neglect</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 6, 2, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irreverentia ipsius obturatio aurium,</span>”
				<i>profanity</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sir. 27, 15</span></i>
			.</div>
